# What this module is

An on-device tool that merges Split APKs (XAPK, APKM, APKS, AAB) into one standalone APK and
re-signs it. The user picks an installed app or a file, chooses which split components to keep,
and starts the merge. The app warns when the app is protected (Google PairIP / Play Integrity,
native signature checks) and offers the "Kill Signature" toggle to get around it.
The default `values/strings.xml` is **Vietnamese**, not English. `values-en` is a translation, so
use it as the pivot language when translating from the Vietnamese source.

Derived: 174 translatable string(s) across 9 locale(s), in `strings.xml`.

## Audience & tone

Power users and modders who know Android technical terms. Short, neutral, technical wording.
Keep technical terms (APK, DEX, PMS Hook, SIGSEGV, syscall) in Latin script, the way the existing
files already do. Badges and chips must fit on one line, so keep them to 1–4 words. Address the
user informally (`vi` bạn, `fr`/`es`/`pt` impersonal or infinitive, `ru` impersonal or вы,
`ko` -습니다 for messages and noun phrases for labels).

## Do not translate

- APK
- Split APK
- Google
- PairIP
- Kill Signature
- Keystore
- Scheme
- libpairipcore.so

